\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Estes\",\"delta\":\"+0.68%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"0.72\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"56.44\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[\"$La6\",\"$La7\",\"$La8\"]}],\"$La9\",\"$Laa\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/heroes/claude\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Claude\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":\"The comp has no front-line. Estes does not create space, he preserves it. With no tank, his peel gets skipped and he gets deleted first.\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"If your draft fails any of those three tests, Estes is the wrong pick and no amount of mechanical skill fixes it.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The one thing that makes Estes work\"]}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Estes trades team mobility for team indestructibility, and every part of his kit services that trade. Moonlight Immersion is not a heal, it is a contract: you agree to keep your ally inside a short tether for a few seconds, and in exchange both of you gain sustained HP regen and bonus Hybrid Defense. Break the tether and the contract voids. That is the whole identity.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The rest of the kit exists to sell that contract harder. The passive, Scripture of the Moon Elf, charges to a full meter and then unloads as an enhanced basic attack that ricochets to nearby enemies with a slow. The charge rate speeds up while linked, which is the game's not-very-subtle way of telling you to keep the link up or stop playing Estes. The ultimate, Blessing of Moon Goddess, is not a healing spike. It is a contract refresh and expansion: every nearby ally gets the link reapplied and enhanced for several seconds, with the instant heal and Hybrid Defense both doubled, whether they had a link or not.\"}]\n84:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Read the kit this way and the decisions become obvious. Linking a dying carry is not a save, it is a down payment on the next several seconds of their life. Ulting when your whole team is healthy is not insurance, it is wasted cooldown. You are the bank, not the ambulance.\"}]\n85:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Laning: the first four minutes\"]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-1\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Help the jungler without touching the buff.\"}],\" Walk in, stand on the creep, let the jungler and minions kill it. Do not auto. Every hit you take on that buff is mana you could have spent in the gold lane. An Estes with a drained mana bar and no link up is worse than an Estes who arrived ten seconds later with mana to spend.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Rotate to gold lane at level 2, not level 1.\"}],\" Take Moonlight Immersion first. Your level-2 power play is the Hybrid Defense bonus, not the heal: a gold-lane marksman riding that extra Hybrid Defense survives trades that otherwise force them to recall. Link, stand behind, let them auto through the extra tankiness.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Cast S1 on cooldown even when the carry is full HP.\"}],\" The link accelerates your passive charge. A full-charge enhanced basic with its ricochet slow is a zoning tool that stops most assassins from walking into the lane. Holding S1 for \\\"when they need healing\\\" is the mistake that makes Estes feel useless early.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n87:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Patch 2.1.88 (\",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/patch-notes\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"patch notes\"}],\") cut his skill mana costs across the board, which eases the early mana crunch but does not erase it. You still cannot afford to dump S1 on a buff camp and arrive in lane empty. The roam lane rotation is where Estes earns his first gold lead or loses the game. If you are still in jungle at 1:30, something has gone wrong.\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The power spike you are farming toward\"]}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The spike is Enchanted Talisman plus Oracle, which usually finishes around the 8-to-10 minute mark on a normal gold curve. Talisman and Oracle both carry cooldown reduction, and Talisman's Magic Mastery passive lifts the cap higher still. Together they push Estes to that cap, where his link cooldown drops low enough to keep near-permanent uptime on his primary carry. Talisman's Mana Spring passive removes the mana pressure that would otherwise punish casting S1 on cooldown.\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Oracle does something more important than the CDR, though. Its Bless passive increases received Shield and HP Regen effects, which amplifies every heal Estes outputs onto the receiving side. In rough terms, Oracle converts one Estes into something closer to 1.25 Estes, and it costs 1860 gold.\"}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"After this spike, Estes stops being a support and starts being a second layer of tankiness. Your carry can stand in the middle of a fight and auto through it. That is what you are farming toward.\"}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-4\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning and target priority\"]}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The reflex when you first pick up Estes is to stand behind the tank. That reflex is wrong. If the tank engages and Estes is on the tank's link, the tank charges forward, Estes does not, the link snaps almost immediately, and the fight starts with zero sustain.\"}]\n8e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Three positioning rules:\"}]\n8f:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-2\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Stand 1 to 2 body-lengths behind your primary carry, always.\"}],\" The carry is your link target. Link range is the only thing that matters for your positioning. If the carry kites backward you kite with them. If the carry steps up you step up.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Save Domain of Moon Goddess for peel, never for engage.\"}],\" The slow only triggers when an enemy walks through the edge. Enemies already inside the domain when it lands are not slowed. Throwing S2 on the enemy team at fight start catches nobody. Drop it between your carry and the incoming diver so the diver has to cross the edge to close distance.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Hold the ult until your carry is at 50 to 60 percent HP with at least two allies in aura range.\"}],\" The ult's value is the refresh plus the doubled link, not the instant heal. Casting it at full HP wastes the enhanced duration. Casting it on a single isolated ally wastes the radial component. Wait for compression.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n90:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-13\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"If your carry is Kimmy you get to push link range further forward because Kimmy does not move. If your carry is \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/heroes/beatrix\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Beatrix\"}],\" in Renner stance you get to stand at maximum link distance and let her poke. If your carry is anyone with a blink, expect to lose the link twice per fight and accept it.\"]}]\n91:[\"$\",\"$Lab\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n92:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: defaults versus flex slots\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Estes runs 3 locked slots and 3 real conversations.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Locked\"}],\": Favor (roam boots passive, the support emblem equivalent), Enchanted Talisman (CDR cap and mana sustain, non-negotiable), Oracle (heal amplification plus layered defenses, covered above). Build in that order.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Flex slot 1: the ult-reset item.\"}],\" Fleeting Time carries cooldown reduction plus its Timestream passive, which shaves a chunk off the ultimate's remaining cooldown on every kill or assist. In grouped deathball comps where you are assist-hunting anyway, that can mean a second team-wide refresh inside one extended fight, which is the correct buy. In slower scaling games where you cannot guarantee the assist, skip it for a second defensive item.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Flex slot 2: the heal-war response.\"}],\" Build Dominance Ice when the enemy has a sustain support (mirror Estes, Rafaela, Angela, Floryn). Its Lifebane passive cuts the healing of anyone who stays close to you, taxing their sustain the same way theirs taxes yours, and Fortress Shield's stacking Hybrid Defense keeps you alive as the focus target. Skip this slot entirely if the enemy has no sustain to fight.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Flex slot 3: the burst counter.\"}],\" Immortality is the default, because Estes is target number one and the brief revive gives your team a peel window. Athena's Shield if the enemy has two or more magic damage threats. Antique Cuirass if the enemy is running two physical assassins.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Flask of the Oasis\"}],\" is a niche buy that deserves its own mention. It shields the target of your heal when they drop below 35% HP and trims your own cooldowns when it fires. It is excellent when paired with a carry who gets burst-checked at low HP (Kimmy, Lesley) and less useful when the carry has natural sustain or burst-evasion tools.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The weakest common default is Enchanted Talisman built fourth or fifth instead of second. Players see the modest stat line and delay it for a flashier item. They never reach the CDR cap, their link sits on its full cooldown all game, and the fights where they should be refreshing the link twice they only refresh it once. Build Talisman before you build anything that looks exciting.\"}],\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb5\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb6\"]\n93:[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Estes\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"94:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 bg-surface-3\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6b\",null,{\"src\":\"https://akmweb.youngjoygame.com/web/svnres/img/test/homepage_2_2_16_1232_1/100_4687eca874feec9017b448a0b9110d65.png\",\"alt\":\"Beatrix - Dawnbreak Soldier\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"priority\":\"$undefined\",\"fetchPriority\":\"$undefined\",\"fill\":true,\"className\":\"object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300\",\"sizes\":\"56px\",\"placeholder\":\"blur\",\"blurDataURL\":\"data:image/svg+xml;b